  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">A <strong id=\"\">Transaction Guarantee</strong> is a setting that users can apply when submitting a transaction to the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Network</strong></a> that guarantees that at least a minimum amount of a certain token be deposited into their account, or the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Network</strong></a> will reject the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-transaction-in-crypto\"><strong id=\"\">transaction</strong></a>.</p><p id=\"\">This helps protect users against unexpected results and sandwich attacks.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-transaction-manifests\"><strong id=\"\">What are Transaction Manifests?</strong></a></li></ul><p id=\"\">‍</p>",
